! mcp_bootstrap_p91.strap -- MCP INITIALIZATION, printed page 91:
! the tail of "ZERO THE I/O REQUEST TBL AND REEL SLOT", the one-line
! note that the unit area table is already generated, and the head of
! "GENERATE THE FILE AREA TABLES".
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.98, header "PAGE NUMBER 91".
!
! Fifty-six printed lines.  THIRTY-FIVE COMPILE; the other twenty-one
! carry only the dash in the STATEMENT column (lines 1-3, 9, 14-16,
! 20, 22, 24-28, 31, 34, 38, 42, 45, 49, 53) or are the boxed banners
! "ZERO THE I/O REQUEST TBL AND REEL SLOT" (line 2), "THE UNIT AREA
! TABLE IS ALREADY GENERATED FOR THIS IOD CARD" (line 15) and
! "GENERATE THE FILE AREA TABLES" (lines 25-27).
!
! CONTIGUOUS BY ADDRESS, AND THE BACKWARD EDGE CLOSES.  First located
! line is 4 at 005154.40, last is 56 at 005210.00 (two half words),
! so printed p.92 must begin at 005211.00.  Every link in between
! closes: each row's location plus one half word per "XXXXXX.NN NN"
! group in its BINARY OUTPUT equals the next row's location, all
! thirty-four links, with no gap and no overlap.  That is what says
! no line fell off the top or the bottom of the render.  Printed
! p.90's last row is its line 56, a single half word at 005154.00
! ("V+I,TMXE,9.0"), and 005154.00 plus one half word is 005154.40 --
! this page's first location, with nothing in between.
!
! WHAT THE PAGE DOES.  Lines 4-13 finish zeroing: the I/O request
! table slot's reel address is loaded, and if non-zero the reel slot
! it points at is zeroed too (T M2AC), then the I/O request table
! slot itself.  The loop walks the table by stepping T MXB a word at
! a time (V+IC) until T LAST+1.0 marks the end, when T MXB is
! reloaded to T IOREQ-1 and the loop drops through to T N5.  Line 17
! (T M1D) starts the per-card work: the IOD card's reference number
! picks a symbolic-I/O location out of T LIMB, that word's unit area
! address goes to T MXEE, and the unit's IOD count is bumped.  Lines
! 29-56 build the file area table for this card: reference number,
! unit area address and file area address into the symbolic I/O
! table, table-of-exits address into the file area table, then the
! mode (card machine or tape), and for tape the disposition and the
! density.  Line 54 reloads the type code and line 55-56 test it for
! DISK.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS -- EVERY ONE TRANSCRIBED ELSEWHERE AND CONFIRMED HERE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Each field offset below is printed in THIS page's own address
! field, and every one matches a deck already in the tree.  Nothing
! here is derived from the assembler.
!
!   T FREEL  000000.34  BU,18   printed pp.56, 62, 69, 70
!   T LAST   000000.22  BU,1    printed pp.57, 58, 62, 65, 66
!                               (line 10 prints 000001.22 -- the
!                                statement is T LAST+1.0)
!   T IOREQ  (8)3373.0          printed pp.48, 57, 58, 65, 66
!                               (line 11's LVI prints 003372.07,
!                                the statement being T IOREQ-1.)
!   T LIMB   (8)2155.0          printed p.83; line 18 prints
!                               002155.00 80  022027.20 10, which is
!                               printed p.89 line 41's row verbatim
!   T UNREF  000000.60  BU,12   printed p.84
!   T IODK   000001.06  BU,12   printed p.84 line 48
!   T IREF   000000.64  BU,12   printed p.84; line 29's whole row is
!                               printed p.89 line 37's row verbatim
!   T IODRN  000000.00  BU,18   printed p.85
!   T IABEX  000000.00  BU,18   printed p.84
!   T TOELO  000002.00  BU,18   printed p.85
!   T ITYCD  000002.74  BU,4    printed pp.84, 89
!   T IMOCD  000006.76  BU,2    printed pp.84, 89
!   T FMODE  000002.60  BU,2    printed p.85
!   T IDSCD  000010.76  BU,2    printed pp.84, 89
!   T REELD  000002.35  BU,3    printed p.85
!   T IDNCD  000007.76  BU,2    printed pp.84, 89
!   T DENMD  000002.33  BU,2    printed p.85
!   the index names T MXB=$3, T MXC=$4, T MXD=$5, T MXG=$8,
!   T MXEE=$9, T MXI=$10, T MXGA=$11 -- all printed p.83, and each
!   confirmed here by the index digit this page's bytes print.
!
! ONE OFF-PAGE BRANCH TARGET, read out of this page's own binary
! column: T M1FA.  Lines 52 and 56 both print 005262 in the address
! field, line 52's B with the ".10" a B prints for a first-half-word
! target (printed p.89 line 40) and line 56's BZAE with the ".36"
! that is p.89 line 51's ".76" with bit 18 cleared.  T M1FA =
! 005262.00.  Printed p.92 will state it outright.
!
! >>> THIS PAGE SETTLES printed p.89's DERIVED T M1D. <<<  That deck
! recovered T M1D = 005162.00 from its line 55's "005162.34 00" and
! the BZB low-field constant ".34".  Line 17 here IS T M1D, and the
! LOCATION column prints 005162.00 beside it.
!
! >>> TWO SPELLINGS IN EARLIER DECKS DO NOT MATCH WHAT THE PAGES
! PRINT. <<<  Recorded here, not changed there:
!   * decks/mcp_bootstrap_p84.strap calls 000001.06 "T IODCK".  Both
!     printed p.84 line 48 and this page's line 23 print "T IODK" --
!     four letters after the T, not five.  This deck writes T IODK.
!   * decks/mcp_bootstrap_p85.strap calls 000002.60 "T FMCDE".  Both
!     printed p.85 line 11 and this page's lines 40 and 44 print
!     "T FMODE", with the closed O of "T ORARC" on the line below it
!     rather than the wide-open C that same name ends with.  The
!     comment on p.85 reads "-FILE MODE".  This deck writes T FMODE.
!
! >>> O AND C IN THE STATEMENT COLUMN. <<<  Line 36's operand prints
! as "TTCELC" at 400 dpi.  Printed p.85 line 8 prints the same symbol
! in its NAME column two lines under "T IODRN", whose O is undamaged,
! and the glyphs match: T TOELO.  Lines 37/46/54's "T ITYCD" and
! lines 39/43's "T IMOCD" were settled the same way, against printed
! p.84's !SYM block, which gives both the address and the width this
! page's own binary column prints.
!
! >>> 0 AND C IN THE HEX BYTE, AND WHY THE EYE CANNOT DO IT HERE.
! <<<  A zero on this page prints OPEN about as often as it prints
! closed.  Crop the two leading zeros of the LOCATION-style octal
! field -- a field that can hold only 0-7, so every round glyph in
! it is certainly a zero -- and at 3600 dpi lines 5, 11, 41 and 52
! print them as two wide C shapes while lines 7, 12 and 13 print the
! first open and the second closed.  Deciding 0 against C by looking
! at one glyph is therefore not possible on this page, and it is how
! "C1" for line 11 and "C0" for line 13 came out of the first read.
!
! WHAT DOES DECIDE IT is the comparison the whole project's rule
! asks for, done against a KNOWN-GOOD INSTANCE IN THE SAME ROW,
! where the ink is the same.  Normalised overlap between the byte's
! first digit and that row's own two octal zeros:
!
!     lines 7, 8, 11, 12, 13, 41, 52   0.70 0.70 0.75 0.73 0.71
!                                      0.84 0.72     -> a zero
!     line  5                          0.55          -> NOT a zero
!     the 8 rows                       0.40-0.57
!     the 3 rows                       0.24-0.40
!     control, zero against zero       0.53-0.84
!
! Every row whose first digit this deck writes as 0 scores at or
! above its own row's zero-against-zero control; line 5, the one row
! that carries a C, falls below every one of them.  Line 56 is below
! that crop and is settled by eye instead: its byte's first glyph is
! a wide C with flat terminals beside the tight closed ovals of its
! own "005262", and it is the same C0 printed p.89's two BZAE rows
! print.  The assembler reproduces all thirty-five rows from the
! STATEMENT text alone, which is the third witness.

! ---- index names, printed p.83 ------------------------------------
TMXB    SYN, $3
TMXC    SYN, $4
TMXD    SYN, $5
TMXG    SYN, $8
TMXEE   SYN, $9
TMXI    SYN, $10
TMXGA   SYN, $11

! ---- words and tables, printed pp.48, 57, 83 ----------------------
TIOREQ  SYN, (8)3373.0
TLIMB   SYN, (8)2155.0

! ---- I/O request table offsets, printed pp.56, 57, 62 -------------
TFREEL  SYN(BU,18), 0.28
TLAST   SYN(BU,1), 0.18

! ---- unit area table offsets, printed p.84 ------------------------
TUNREF  SYN(BU,12), 0.48
TIODK   SYN(BU,12), 1.6

! ---- IOD card breakdown table offsets, printed p.84 ---------------
TIABEX  SYN(BU,18), 0.0
TIREF   SYN(BU,12), 0.52
TITYCD  SYN(BU,4), 2.60
TIMOCD  SYN(BU,2), 6.62
TIDNCD  SYN(BU,2), 7.62
TIDSCD  SYN(BU,2), 8.62

! ---- file area table offsets, printed p.85 ------------------------
TIODRN  SYN(BU,18), 0.0
TTOELO  SYN(BU,18), 2.0
TDENMD  SYN(BU,2), 2.27
TREELD  SYN(BU,3), 2.29
TFMODE  SYN(BU,2), 2.48

! ---- off page, read out of THIS page's binary column --------------
TM1FA   SYN, (8)5262.0

        SLC, (8)5154.40

! ---- ZERO THE I/O REQUEST TBL AND REEL SLOT (continued) ----------
        L, TFREEL(TMXB), 46          ! line 4  -GET THE FIRST REEL ADDRESS
        BRZ, TM2AC                   ! line 5  -NO REEL
        LV, TMXGA, $R                ! line 6
        Z, 0.0(TMXGA)                ! line 7  -ZERO THE REEL SLOT
TM2AC   Z, 0.0(TMXB)                 ! line 8  -ZERO THE I/O REQ TBL SLOT
        BZB, TLAST+1.0(TMXB), TM1DB  ! line 10 -IF NOT LAST ENTRY IN THE
                                      !          I/O REQ TBL
        LVI, TMXB, TIOREQ-1.         ! line 11
TM1DB   V+IC, TMXB, 1.0              ! line 12
        B, TN5                       ! line 13

! ---- THE UNIT AREA TABLE IS ALREADY GENERATED FOR THIS IOD CARD --
TM1D    L, TUNREF(TMXG), 46          ! line 17 -GET THE REF NO.
        +(BU,18), TLIMB, 46          ! line 18 -COMPUTE SYMB. I/O LOC
                                      !          ADDRESS
        LV, TMXG, $R                 ! line 19
        LV, TMXEE, 0.0(TMXG)         ! line 21 -GET UNIT AREA ADDRESS
TN5     M+1, TIODK(TMXEE)            ! line 23 -ADD TO IOD COUNT

! ---- GENERATE THE FILE AREA TABLES -------------------------------
        L, TIREF(TMXI), 46           ! line 29 -GENERATE LOC OF SYMB I/O
                                      !          LOC WORD
        CM0101, TIODRN(TMXD), 46     ! line 30 -STORE REF NO. IN FILE
                                      !          AREA TABLE
        SV, TMXEE, 0.0(TMXC)         ! line 32 -STORE UNIT AREA ADD IN
                                      !          SYMB I/O TB
        SV, TMXD, 0.32(TMXC)         ! line 33 -STORE FILE AREA ADD IN
                                      !          SYMB I/O TB
        C0011, TIABEX(TMXI)          ! line 35 -GET TABLE OF EXITS ADDRESS
        CM0101, TTOELO(TMXD)         ! line 36 -PLACE IN FILE AREA TABLE
        BB, TITYCD(TMXI), TM1FUZ     ! line 37 -IF TAPE
        LF, TIMOCD-1.0(TMXI)         ! line 39 -GET CARD MACHINE MODE
        CM0101, TFMODE(TMXD)         ! line 40
        B, TM1FAZ                    ! line 41
TM1FUZ  LF, TIMOCD(TMXI)             ! line 43 -GET THE TAPE MODE
        SF, TFMODE(TMXD)             ! line 44
        BZB, TITYCD(TMXI), TM1FAZ    ! line 46 -IF THE EQUIP IS NOT TAPE
        C0011, TIDSCD(TMXI)          ! line 47 -GET THE REEL DISP
        CM0101, TREELD(TMXD)         ! line 48
        C0011, TIDNCD(TMXI)          ! line 50 -GET GIVEN DENSITY
        CM0101, TDENMD(TMXD)         ! line 51
        B, TM1FA                     ! line 52
TM1FAZ  L, TITYCD(TMXI)              ! line 54
        KFI(BU,4), 1                 ! line 55 -LOOK FOR DISK
        BZAE, TM1FA                  ! line 56 -IF NOT DISK

